            {
              "id": "1ff49f82-3634-4782-848c-60fbe57aa472",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>The Play of the Self </strong></em>is a collection of essays edited by Ronald Bogue &amp; Mihai I. Sparisou, published by SUNY Press, September 8, 1994."
            },
            {
              "id": "975458a4-afdb-4b2f-a522-b8940b692be9",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "e1cc1a55-f519-4676-b2f0-36c30236a421",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>This interdisciplinary study explores the relationship between play and mimesis in the constitution and dissolution of the individual and social self. The volume is divided into three sections, the first of which focuses on the </em><a href=\"#/mimesis\"><em>mimetic</em></a><em>-</em><a href=\"#/ludus\"><em>ludic</em></a><em> foundations of mind, memory, and desire; the second on the social and psychological self as agent of playful performance and product of cultural codes; and the third on the interplay of psyche, image, and power in literary and artistic representations of the self. The subjects of the individual studies vary widely, from the interrelation of power and play in Orlando Furioso to the ludic foundations of cognition to the concept of the self in Foucault and </em><a href=\"#/exploring-videogames-with-deleuze-and-guattari\"><em>Deleuze</em></a><em>.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "ad8efc5b-dc01-42c6-8f5e-594dcea1c91e",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
          ]
